      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i keep getting an \"Access Denied\" error when my lambda function tries to write logs to this s3 bucket. i thought i had the permissions right but it's still failing. can u look at this policy and tell me what i missed?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The policy looks correct from a permissions standpoint. However, remember to attach this policy as a bucket policy to the S3 bucket where your Lambda function has access — not the Lambda function's execution role. Make sure your Lambda function's policy has permissions to list and write to the S3 bucket's log path. Also, check that your S3 bucket's public access settings do not block anonymous access, as it might affect the logs. If so, temporarily change those settings to \"ACLs enabled\" and retry. If the error persists, it could be due to networking issues, so verify your Lambda's IAM role, S3 bucket configuration, and VPC connectivity.",
